description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Critical Systems Engineer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EdgeConneX is in search for its next Critical Systems Engineer.&amp;nbsp; The Critical Systems Engineer is a member of the Operations Support team and provides Level 2 escalation support from our Critical Systems Coordinators. This role brings deep expertise in mission-critical electrical and mechanical infrastructure and supports the reliability, safety, and efficiency of EdgeConneX data centers. The CSE serves as a technical authority for the maintenance and operational oversight of critical systems, collaborating closely with critical systems teams, field operations, vendors, and corporate engineering teams to ensure reliability, safety, and consistency across data center operations. This position reports to the Critical Systems Manager and can be based in the cities listed in our posting.&amp;nbsp; This position will require up to 25% travel to support various maintenance initiatives and trainings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: Amsterdam, the Netherlands or Dublin, Ireland&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preventive and corrective maintenance programs across data centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support reliability improvement initiatives and operational readiness activities, including review of system performance, equipment reliability trends, and process effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and participate in post-event root cause analysis (RCA) processes to support continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, review, and approve Methods of Procedure (MOPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and maintenance of Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Emergency Operating Procedures (EOPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and manage field-related projects as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for facility improvements, including efficiency and PUE optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with applicable codes, regulations, and company directives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide escalation support and technical consultation as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties as assigned by management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor maintenance activities and ensure SLA compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;CMMS / Asset Manager Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure complete and accurate asset sheets are delivered in Asset Manager from the Construction Management and/or Engineering Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate and correct asset data, including ELI codes, serial numbers, and model numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine contact information for maintenance vendors and manufacturers as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map equipment to maintenance vendors and ensure maintenance contracts are in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Site Engineers to determine maintenance schedules and activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Load assets and maintenance schedules into CMMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mission-critical data center equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of electrical systems (UPS, generators, switchgear, etc) and mechanical systems (air handlers, rooftop units, pumps, fans)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fire alarm and suppression systems (FIKE) &amp;amp; Building Management Systems (BMS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preventive maintenance program creation and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of DCIM and CMMS systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Word and Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, prioritization, and multitasking skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate technical information verbally and in writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable of leading and managing vendors, technicians, and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates who also have a general IT awareness of servers, networking, and peripheral equipment are highly encouraged to apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Education and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8 years of professional relevant mission-critical MEP experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with data centers, critical facilities, UPS systems, emergency generators, or electrical switchgear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates who either possess a degree or Industrial Technology trade school certification along with verifiable technical training are highly encouraged to apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Travel&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will require regular travel (approximately 25%) to manage additional Data Centers across EMEA.&amp;nbsp; There will also be travel for annual and quarterly company meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: Data Center Facility Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; (Cikarang)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Center Facility Manager will be responsible for all day-to-day operations of our newest data center in Cikarang, leading a pro-active approach to maintenance and procedures, managing delivery of the services level committed to ECX Clients. This role reports to our Campus Manager and Regional Director, Data Center Operations for all of APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Center Facility Manager should be an experienced manager with extensive data center facilities maintenance, vendor management, technical engineering, and interpersonal skills. Technical, commercial, and managerial skills will be prime requirements.&amp;nbsp; The Data Center Facility Manager will have an intimate understanding of the customer service requirements and expectations; and the MEP infrastructure on the Data Centers of EdgeConneX. This position will be based in Cikarang and require onsite support 5 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for overseeing the operation and maintenance of the M&amp;amp;E Services (e.g power, cooling, space, and asset inventory) within the Data Center in a 24/7 mission critical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership and guidance to teams, ensuring the performance of the team and delivery of EdgeConneX&#39;s Service Level Agreement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee day-to-day operations and manage a team of engineers, including outsourced contractors; and to be on standby with 24/7 on-call emergency response and availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain M&amp;amp;E Services infrastructure and coordinate with vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and plan for MEP preventive, corrective, and predictive maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle client inquiries and requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with project development teams during DC design and development phases for new data centers, ensuring all operational requirements are defined and implemented correctly during constructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in all testing and commissioning of systems, and support Regional leadership to plan and manage the transition from construction to stable operations of the DC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit qualified engineers/technicians and manage their performance, morale, and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure company and data center operations process and procedures are followed and meet internal/external audit standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule and supervise the performance of routine maintenance and emergency repairs on all building services and M&amp;amp;E&amp;nbsp;data center equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement company occupational health and safety program on site, ensuring strict compliance by employees and contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions to operate existing systems efficiently, including their lifecycle cost, with conclusions and suitable approaches to problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage facility budget for maintenance, repairs, capital, and general operating costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;u&gt;Maintenance Management:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and maintain the mandatory legal requirements in connection with the operation and maintenance of the data center .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop maintenance master plan for planned preventive maintenance, cyclical parts replacement, major maintenance, and overhaul works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop maintenance standards, procedures, and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct performance appraisal for subcontractors, vendors, and suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure no violations of Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety legislations and security policies, procedures, guidelines, and house rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instill a culture of ownership, high standard of care, expertise and diligence with all key personnel, subcontractors, vendors, and suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct supplier audits on subcontractors, vendors, and suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;u&gt;Incident Management:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the first level of escalation to ensure incidents are resolved within the duration as stipulated under the client SLA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, approve and submit incident report with root cause analysis as stipulated under client SLA timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, approve and submit Facilities Monthly Report as stipulated under Client SLA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, approve and submit quotations for corrective maintenance, improvement projects, customer installs, and ad-hoc works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform any other duties as instructed by management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in both written and spoken English and Bahasa Indonesia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be at the data center location within &lt;strong&gt;30-45 minutes&lt;/strong&gt; of being called in for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently with minimum of supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills; able to communicate effectively and in a professional manner with team, clients, vendors, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good organizational skills with the ability to maintain all facility related documentation through detailed and carefully-written submissions and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects/responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive mentality to meet committed timelines, leveraging peer assistance/input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and effective team player in working with various disciplines and peer groups; can cover all gamut of tasks required to ‘getting a job done.’&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Education&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant work experience in a data center or other mission critical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MEP Operational expertise with critical facility equipment/ system including, but not limited to transformers, generators, DRUPS, UPS, PDU, Chillers, CRAH and Fire Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of management experience in a data center environment with a track record of managing people, process, and systems to a high level of efficiency and strong performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Electrical, Mechanical or related Engineering studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety Training for Operational Supervisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: Data Center SME Mechanical Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;SME Mechanical &lt;/strong&gt;will support and lead the local data center site team on advanced mechanical engineering duties within the JKT datacenter campus based in JKT Indonesia. This position reports to the Data Center Facility Manager and requires someone to be onsite daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight of critical infrastructure and building mechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate critical infrastructure to include Fan Wall Units, CRAH’s, CRAC’s, Chillers, Humidification Systems, De-humidification Systems, RTU’s, CDU’s, and Water Purification Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue identification and resolution through RCA and remediation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordination and oversite of maintenance and corrective activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordination and oversite of customer requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System analysis and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of self-performing PM/CM activities in accordance with ECX standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development and execution of MOP’s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise on-site subcontractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the regional team as required in support of customer reporting and QBRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent and accurate updates to tickets, WO’s, and associated communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed knowledge of critical infrastructure - to include Fan Wall Units, CRAH’s, CRAC’s, Chillers, Humidification Systems, De-humidification Systems, RTU’s, CDU’s, and Water Purification Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and assess single line diagrams, technical manuals and engineering plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience carrying out MOP/EOP/SOP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communications, both written and verbal, coordinating with local and regional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to organizational excellence and constant awareness to seek opportunities to improve processes/quality of deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and manage a breadth of responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to meet committed timelines, leveraging assistance/input from team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and effective team player working with various disciplines and peer groups; can cover all gamut of tasks required to ‘getting a job done.’&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Education&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing data center mechanical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience leading a team of service technicians focused in mechanical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, demonstrated interest in data center technology with a passion for continued learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge and experience in supporting a fast-paced, demanding environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any experience working in pre-deployment phases of a data center, i.e. pre-construction or construction environments would make a candidate stand out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates possessing direct experience in leading mechanical engineering efforts at a hyperscale data center facility are highly encouraged to apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;321&quot; data-end=&quot;378&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;324&quot; data-end=&quot;376&quot;&gt;Title: Data Center Subject Matter Expert (Power)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;379&quot; data-end=&quot;408&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;379&quot; data-end=&quot;392&quot;&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Dublin, Ireland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;410&quot; data-end=&quot;807&quot;&gt;The Data Center Subject Matter Expert (Power) will serve as an in-house expert for power systems and is responsible for the critical operations and maintenance of electrical and mechanical infrastructure within EdgeConneX data centers. This role reports to the Director of Data Center Operations and plays a key role in ensuring safe, reliable, and continuous operations across assigned sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;814&quot; data-end=&quot;845&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;817&quot; data-end=&quot;845&quot;&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;847&quot; data-end=&quot;3023&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;847&quot; data-end=&quot;951&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;849&quot; data-end=&quot;951&quot;&gt;Manage projects and operational activities to support customer requirements and ensure 100% uptime&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;847&quot; data-end=&quot;951&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;849&quot; data-end=&quot;951&quot;&gt;Initiate and support projects to improve operational processes and procedures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1032&quot; data-end=&quot;1265&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1034&quot; data-end=&quot;1265&quot;&gt;Ensure the safe, effective, and efficient delivery of critical planned maintenance, in compliance with all EdgeConneX standards and procedures, leveraging qualified contractor and vendor resources with a strong focus on quality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1266&quot; data-end=&quot;1420&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1268&quot; data-end=&quot;1420&quot;&gt;Ensure the Director of Data Center Operations is fully informed of all critical planned, corrective, and emergent work occurring within the data centers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1421&quot; data-end=&quot;1575&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1423&quot; data-end=&quot;1575&quot;&gt;Plan and execute customer-requested work in a timely manner, providing clear status updates to both customers and the Director of Data Center Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1576&quot; data-end=&quot;1893&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1578&quot; data-end=&quot;1638&quot;&gt;In coordination with the Director of Data Center Operations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1641&quot; data-end=&quot;1893&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1641&quot; data-end=&quot;1766&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1643&quot; data-end=&quot;1766&quot;&gt;Plan work on critical single-line electrical equipment in accordance with the Planned Preventive Maintenance (PPM) schedule&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1769&quot; data-end=&quot;1893&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1771&quot; data-end=&quot;1893&quot;&gt;Develop maintenance roadmaps for approval by the Director of Data Center Operations and/or the appointed Authorised Person&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;1894&quot; data-end=&quot;2003&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1896&quot; data-end=&quot;2003&quot;&gt;Manage and oversee testing of mission-critical power equipment in accordance with EMEA and global standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2004&quot; data-end=&quot;2100&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2006&quot; data-end=&quot;2100&quot;&gt;Ensure all contractor and vendor work is properly logged and tracked within EdgeConneX systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2101&quot; data-end=&quot;2236&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2103&quot; data-end=&quot;2236&quot;&gt;Ensure all work performed by contractors and vendors is executed strictly in accordance with approved Methods of Procedure (MOPs)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2237&quot; data-end=&quot;2403&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2239&quot; data-end=&quot;2403&quot;&gt;Respond during normal working hours to alarms, critical incidents, and emergencies, communicating clearly, calmly, and in line with the site Emergency Response Plan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2404&quot; data-end=&quot;2585&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2406&quot; data-end=&quot;2585&quot;&gt;Proactively identify opportunities to improve equipment reliability, quality, and efficiency, including initiatives that deliver cost savings without compromising safety or uptime&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2586&quot; data-end=&quot;2712&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2588&quot; data-end=&quot;2712&quot;&gt;Administer project-related changes accurately and in a timely manner, in accordance with EdgeConneX processes and procedures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2713&quot; data-end=&quot;2818&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2715&quot; data-end=&quot;2818&quot;&gt;Collaborate effectively with internal teams across Operations, Engineering, and other functional groups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2819&quot; data-end=&quot;2925&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2821&quot; data-end=&quot;2925&quot;&gt;Provide timely on-site response during emergencies to ensure personnel safety and operational continuity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;2926&quot; data-end=&quot;3023&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2928&quot; data-end=&quot;3023&quot;&gt;Monitor multiple sites to ensure compliance with safety, operational, and performance standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;3030&quot; data-end=&quot;3066&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;3030&quot; data-end=&quot;3066&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3033&quot; data-end=&quot;3066&quot;&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3068&quot; data-end=&quot;3828&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3068&quot; data-end=&quot;3242&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3070&quot; data-end=&quot;3242&quot;&gt;Strong technical knowledge of data center power systems, including transformers, generators, switchgear, UPS systems, ATS/STS units, RPPs, and associated infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3243&quot; data-end=&quot;3394&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3245&quot; data-end=&quot;3394&quot;&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to lead teams and coordinate effectively across disciplines to drive work to closure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3395&quot; data-end=&quot;3473&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3397&quot; data-end=&quot;3473&quot;&gt;Demonstrated commitment to operational excellence and continuous improvement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3474&quot; data-end=&quot;3579&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3476&quot; data-end=&quot;3579&quot;&gt;Proven ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects and responsibilities in a dynamic environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3580&quot; data-end=&quot;3668&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3582&quot; data-end=&quot;3668&quot;&gt;Ability to meet committed timelines by leveraging collaboration and support from peers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3669&quot; data-end=&quot;3765&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3671&quot; data-end=&quot;3765&quot;&gt;Strong team player with the ability to work across multiple disciplines and stakeholder groups&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3766&quot; data-end=&quot;3828&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3768&quot; data-end=&quot;3828&quot;&gt;High attention to detail and strong documentation discipline&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;3835&quot; data-end=&quot;3864&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h4 data-start=&quot;3835&quot; data-end=&quot;3864&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3838&quot; data-end=&quot;3864&quot;&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3866&quot; data-end=&quot;4701&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3866&quot; data-end=&quot;4045&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3868&quot; data-end=&quot;4045&quot;&gt;Relevant technical qualification at NFQ Level 6–8 (e.g., Electrical or Mechanical Engineering, Building Services Engineering, Facilities Management) or equivalent experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4046&quot; data-end=&quot;4177&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4048&quot; data-end=&quot;4177&quot;&gt;10+ years of progressive experience supporting critical facilities, data centers, or comparable mission-critical environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4178&quot; data-end=&quot;4344&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4180&quot; data-end=&quot;4344&quot;&gt;Electrical Authorised Person / Competent Person certification in accordance with Irish or UK standards (e.g., Safe Electric, HV/LV Authorisation, or equivalent)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4345&quot; data-end=&quot;4433&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4347&quot; data-end=&quot;4433&quot;&gt;Formal mechanical and/or electrical training, with a strong focus on power systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4434&quot; data-end=&quot;4595&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4436&quot; data-end=&quot;4595&quot;&gt;Health &amp;amp; Safety training appropriate for supervisory roles (e.g., Safe Pass, IOSH Managing Safely, NEBOSH, or equivalent; OSHA30 accepted where applicable)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4596&quot; data-end=&quot;4701&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4598&quot; data-end=&quot;4701&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience operating within live data center or other critical infrastructure environments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Center Subject Matter Expert (Power)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;SME &lt;/strong&gt;will be an in-house expert for Power, and responsible for the critical operations and maintenance of mechanical and electrical equipment in data centers. This position reports to Director of Data Center Operations&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage projects to accommodate towards customers 100% uptime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate projects for operational processes and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ensuring the safe, effective, and efficient delivery of critical planned maintenance, that meets all EdgeConneX standards and procedures, by leveraging competent contractor/vendor resources with attention to quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures that the Director of Data Center Operations is fully informed and briefed on all critical planned and corrective work occurring in the data centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans and implements customer-requested work in a timely manner. Ensures that the customer and Director of Data Center Operations are informed on the status and details of the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In concert with the Director of Data Center Operations:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans work on critical 1-line equipment according to Planned Preventive Maintenance Schedule, including roadmap to be approved by Director of Data Center Operations and/or Nominated person in control of an electrical installation. (Dutch:” Installatieverantwoordelijke”)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages all testing of mission critical equipment on the sites according to EMEA/Global standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for guidelines that all work being done by contractors/vendors is logged in EdgeConneX systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for guidelines that all work being done by contractors/vendors is being done in accordance with the approved Method of Procedure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During normal working hours, responds to alarms, critical situations, and emergencies in a proper and timely manner. Responsible for communicating in a calm and clear manner and in accordance with the emergency response plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes initiative to ensure that quality and efficiency standards are raised for all the equipment in the data centers. This includes finding ways to deliver cost savings to EdgeConneX without sacrificing quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administers in a correct and timely manner all changes due to projects in accordance with all process and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works effectively and efficiently with others inside the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Emergencies, is responsible for the timely response to ensure safety and operational continuity on sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors multiple sites to ensure that safety standards are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Electrical in the Data center environment including transformers, generators, switchgear, UPS systems, ATS &amp;amp; STS units, RPP units, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communications, both written and verbal, in leading teams and coordinating with peers and other disciplines on driving projects/issues to closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to organizational excellence and constant awareness to seek opportunities to improve processes/quality of deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects/responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to meet committed timelines, leveraging assistance/input from peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and effective team player in working with various disciplines and peer groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Education&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education level complied with by WEB level 4 (WEB = Dutch Adult and Vocational Training Act) with at least 10-years of experience or HBO (B-Sc./B-Eng.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LV/HV authorized to switch Certificate (NEN3140-NEN3840)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical and/or Electrical training/education, with particular focus in Power&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety for Operational Supervisors training (VCA and OSHA30)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant work experience in a data center or other critical environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30% of the time within EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;EdgeConneX is seeking a hands-on visionary&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Data Center Electrical Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to define the electrical architecture for our next-generation global data center standard. In this high-impact role, you will research and evaluate current and emerging technologies, translate innovation into pragmatic, future‑proof designs, and set clear, scalable standards that balance build complexity, cost, and schedule. You’ll author and maintain design guidelines, templates, and best practices that our internal project engineering teams and external EPC partners will use worldwide. The ideal candidate brings deep technical rigor and international experience, yet embraces that there are multiple valid paths to a great solution—able to articulate trade-offs, align stakeholders, and drive consensus across diverse customer requirements. If you’re excited to shape industry-leading architectures, contribute to community initiatives advancing data center technology, and deliver adaptable solutions at global scale, we’d love to meet you. This Individual Contributor position can be based in either one of our offices in Virginia and Colorado or be based remotely in the U.S. or countries in EMEA where we already have infrastructure.&amp;nbsp; It will require 25% travel globally as it will support all of our Design Engineering teams globally.&amp;nbsp; For now, this position will report to our Head of Global Data Center Design Engineering based in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define Electrical Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and standardize electrical designs for EdgeConneX data centers, ensuring scalability, reliability, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research &amp;amp; Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay ahead of industry trends and community initiatives, evaluating new technologies and systems to incorporate best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Create, maintain, and update design standards, guidelines, and templates to provide clear direction for internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with internal project engineering teams and external EPC partners to ensure alignment and successful implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution-Oriented Approach:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver flexible solutions that meet diverse customer requirements while maintaining consistency with EdgeConneX standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate ideas effectively, establish actionable plans, drive consensus, and secure buy-in across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering (or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10 years in large-scale (minimum 20MW) data center electrical design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience on international projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of electrical systems, power distribution, redundancy strategies, and emerging data center technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate complex challenges and propose multiple viable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving consensus among diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Required Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global standards and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with EPC firms and managing large-scale deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for innovation and continuous improvement in data center design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$215,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: Principal Data Center Mechanical (Design) Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EdgeConneX is seeking a visionary &lt;strong&gt;Principal Data Center Mechanical Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to define the mechanical architecture for our next-generation global data center standard. In this high-impact role, you will research and evaluate current and emerging cooling technologies, translate innovation into pragmatic, future‑proof designs, and set clear, scalable standards that balance build complexity, cost, and schedule. You’ll author and maintain design guidelines, templates, and best practices that our internal project engineering teams and external EPC partners will use worldwide. The ideal candidate brings deep technical rigor and international experience, yet embraces that there are multiple valid paths to a great solution—able to articulate trade-offs, align stakeholders, and drive consensus across diverse customer requirements. If you’re excited to shape industry-leading architectures, contribute to community initiatives advancing data center technology, and deliver adaptable solutions at global scale, we’d love to meet you. This Individual Contributor position can be based in either one of our offices in Virginia and Colorado or be based remotely in the U.S. or countries in EMEA where we already have infrastructure.&amp;nbsp; It will require 25% travel globally as it will support all of our Design Engineering teams globally.&amp;nbsp; For now, this position will report to our Head of Global Data Center Design Engineering based in the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define Mechanical Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and standardize mechanical designs for EdgeConneX data centers, ensuring efficiency, scalability, and sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research &amp;amp; Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay ahead of industry trends and community initiatives, evaluating new cooling technologies, energy efficiency strategies, and mechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Create, maintain, and update design standards, guidelines, and templates to provide clear direction for internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with internal project engineering teams and external EPC partners to ensure alignment and successful implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution-Oriented Approach:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver flexible solutions that meet diverse customer requirements while maintaining consistency with EdgeConneX standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate ideas effectively, establish actionable plans, drive consensus, and secure buy-in across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering (or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 10 years in large-scale data center mechanical design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience on international projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of HVAC systems, cooling technologies, energy efficiency strategies, and emerging mechanical innovations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate complex challenges and propose multiple viable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving consensus among diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Required Attributes:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global standards and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with EPC firms and managing large-scale deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for innovation and continuous improvement in data center design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$195,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: Regional Manager, APAC Data Center Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Regional Manager, APAC Data Center Operations&lt;/strong&gt; will work directly with the Regional Directors to monitor, maintain and support EdgeConneX data centers throughout the APAC region. This requires leading scheduled preventive maintenance activities, performing unscheduled maintenance, and supporting any customer requests.&amp;nbsp; He or she will also help manage facility expansions and improvement, new MEP capacity expansions or repairs, and utility upgrades. While an IT background could be helpful to complement the leadership needed, the background coveted is in MEP.&amp;nbsp; This position reports to the Regional Director of APAC Data Center Operations and will be expected to work closely with the other Regional Managers (across other regions), peers in other departments, Customer Installation Project Managers and with contract vendors to accomplish their tasks.&amp;nbsp; While this position can be based in Cyberjaya or Johor, travel could be as much as 50%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Regional Directors in implementing and managing the Preventive Maintenance program at each of our sites and act as on-site lead for any emergency maintenance done at the EDCs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all customer SLA requirements are met and maintained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of highly skilled engineers. Support hiring activities for new developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) and other systems to ensure they are up to date and have the correct information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage, supervise, and evaluate contract technical labor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying areas of improvement to our existing facilities, particularly efficiency and PUE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and improve the security of data center facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct routine, ongoing assessment of the building systems operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring compliance with all safety procedures as well as utilization of protective equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain ongoing communication with tenants, owners, property management and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel can be up to 50% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to organizational excellence and constant awareness to seek opportunities to improve processes/quality of deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to successfully prioritize and manage multiple projects and responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to meet committed timelines, leveraging assistance/input from peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and effective team player in working with various disciplines and peer groups; can cover all gamut of tasks required to ‘getting a job done’&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high level of commitment to customer service to both co-workers and clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to respond effectively, verbally and in writing, to sensitive issues, complex inquiries or complaints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interact effectively with managers, clients, customers and the general public&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate company goals/KPI’s towards the team and bring the team to the next level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Education&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in facility operations or engineering functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Management function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with power- and mechanical equipment, HV and LV switchgear and different brands of generators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant data center operations experience, to include detailed knowledge of UPS/PDU/RPP/CRAC/Generator and Security and Fire/Life Safety systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multiple PM cycles for Data Center equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with trouble ticketing systems and Method-of-Procedure processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to recommend improvements to dispatch and reporting processes and systems used for contract technical labor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Change Management and CMMS systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehend, analyze, and interpret complex project documents, including AutoCAD, Visio and PDF documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and evaluate maintenance procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop installation standards and project tracking/management documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the Construction or Real Estate environments a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education level - Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety for Operational Supervisors (OSHA 30)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title: Senior &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Center Facility Engineer (Cyberjaya, Malaysia)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In close consultation with Data Center management, the Senior Field Engineer will contribute to the maintenance of the technical installations and infrastructure on the Data Centers of EdgeConneX. This position will be based onsite in Cyberjaya, Malaysia, and report to the Data Center Facility Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ensuring the safe, effective, and efficient delivery of planned maintenance, that meets all EdgeConneX standards and procedures, by leveraging competent contractor/vendor resources with attention to quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans and implements customer requested work in a timely manner. Ensures that the customer and company management are informed on the status and details of the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;During normal working hours, responds to alarms, critical situations, and emergencies in a proper and timely manner. Responsible for communicating in a calm and clear manner and in accordance with the emergency response plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures that company management is fully informed and briefed on all planned and corrective work occurring in the Data Center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In concert with the operations:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plans work on equipment according to Planned Preventive Maintenance Schedule, including roadmap to be approved by Manager of Operations and/or Nominated person in control of an electrical installation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares detailed Method of Procedure to be approved by Operations Manager and/or nominated person in control of an electrical installation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organizes all testing of mission critical equipment on the site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ensuring that all work being done by contractors/vendors is logged in EdgeConneX systems and is in accordance with the approved Method of Procedure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ensuring that all work being done by contractors/vendors is completed per MOP, systems is functioning, and workplace is clean.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Will take initiative to ensure that quality and efficiency standards are raised for all the equipment in the Data Center. This includes finding ways to delivery cost savings to EdgeConneX without sacrificing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership during incidents and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train new hires on DC installations and operations maintenance and standards, customers service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finds ways to increase energy efficiency without sacrificing continuity or uptime of the site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administers in a correct and timely manner all executed work in accordance with all process and Procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works effectively and efficiently with others inside the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Emergencies, is responsible for the timely response to ensure safety and operational continuity on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is constantly monitoring works on site to ensure that safety standards are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This job requires 24/7 on-call support&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Knowledge, Skills &amp;amp; Abilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and Bahasa Indonesia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be at the data center location within &lt;strong&gt;30 minutes&lt;/strong&gt; of being called in for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge and operational experience of Mechanical and Electrical systems in use in the Data Center environment including transformers, generators, switchgear, UPS systems, ATS &amp;amp; STS units, RPP units, chillers, CRAC/CRAH units and fire systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of HVAC principles and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communications, both written and verbal, in leading teams and coordinating with peers and other disciplines on driving projects/issues to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to organizational excellence and constant awareness to seek opportunities to improve processes/quality of deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects/responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb ability to meet committed timelines, leveraging assistance/input from peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong and effective team player in working with various disciplines and peer groups; can cover all gamut of tasks required to ‘getting a job done.’&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Education&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education level complied with Local standards minimal a M&amp;amp;E or related technical education at Degree Level at minimum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant M&amp;amp;E training/education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past Safety Completed for Operational Supervisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant work experience in a data center or other mission critical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of supervisory/lead experience in MEP or a related field, preferably within a data center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX believes inclusion – of thought, backgrounds and experiences – affects all that we do, from our employees to the solutions we deliver. Our goal is to create an environment where embracing differences helps deepen the lives and work experience of our employees, enhances our innovation and creativity, and enriches our involvement in our communities. EdgeConneX is an equal employment opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, as well as any other category protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;EdgeConneX offers a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;For more information on how we process your data, visit our Data Privacy Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.edgeconnex.com/privacy-policy/#:~:text=Our%20goal%20is%20to%20be,to%20Personal%20Data%20we%20process.&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;­Led by an experienced management team and supported by a strong investor group, including large and experienced institutions and strategic partners, EdgeConneX offers a dynamic, fast-paced work environment where we are bringing flexibility, proximity, power, and connectivity to some of the world’s key businesses. With major offices in Herndon, Denver, and Amsterdam, we have a global footprint and a unified team of employees committed to providing a premier customer experience and delivering the full spectrum of data center solutions, from core to edge, like no other data center provider can do.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Focused on driving innovation and helping our customers define and deliver their own unique vision for the Edge, at any scale, in any market worldwide, for any requirement, we are building tomorrow’s data center infrastructure, today for some of the world’s most demanding Network, Content, and Cloud customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technical (Data Centre Design) Program Manager will oversee the end-to-end delivery of data centre projects, including design review, construction, commissioning, and operational handover. This role ensures that all MEP engineering, construction, and operational requirements are met on time, within budget, and according to quality and compliance standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position involves close coordination with multi-disciplinary teams — mechanical electrical, plumbing (MEP), civil, electrical, IT infrastructure, security and operations — to deliver hyperscale, colocation, and enterprise data centres.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for candidates with &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;strong mechanical and electrical expertise&lt;/span&gt;, hands-on experience in hyperscale and Tier III+ data centres, and proven project management leadership.&amp;nbsp; This position is based in Johor as a hybrid onsite structure is needed, and will require at least 30% travel to the other site (Cyberjaya) and other regional travel when key meetings or coverage is needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Key Roles &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Management &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full project lifecycle: planning, design, procurement, construction, commissioning, energization, and handover.&lt;br&gt;Develop, monitor, and maintain master project schedules, budgets, and resource plans.&lt;br&gt;• Establish project governance framework, reporting cadence, and executive dashboards.&lt;br&gt;• Identify project risks, maintain risk registers, implement mitigation strategies, and escalate critical issues.&lt;br&gt;• Manage contract administration, variation orders (VO), claims assessment, and commercial negotiations.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure contractor compliance with contractual milestones, performance guarantees, and LD provisions.&lt;br&gt;• Support procurement strategy including evaluation of EPC / D&amp;amp;B / CM delivery models.&lt;br&gt;• Manage long-lead equipment procurement (transformers, generators, UPS, chillers) including FAT oversight.&lt;br&gt;• Prepare and present progress reports, KPIs, cost forecasts, and milestone updates to senior management and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;2. Engineering &amp;amp; Technical Oversight&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, approve, and coordinate technical designs: electrical, mechanical, HVAC, fire protection, security, and IT infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;Validate system redundancy (N+1, N+2, 2N, 2N+1) and operational reliability requirements.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure compliance with local regulations, utility requirements, and international standards (Uptime Tier III/IV, NFPA, IEC, TIA, ISO).&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate with utility providers (e.g., TNB or regional utilities) for grid interconnection, energization, and regulatory approvals.&lt;br&gt;• Oversee HV/MV infrastructure delivery, protection coordination, and energization strategy.&lt;br&gt;• Supervise Testing &amp;amp; Commissioning (Level 1–5) including IST, FMEA validation, black building tests, and reliability verification.&lt;br&gt;• Review power system studies (short circuit, load flow, arc flash) and reliability analysis.&lt;br&gt;• Oversee vendor, contractor, and consultant performance to meet technical specifications and project objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;3. Team Leadership &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor CAPEX budgets, cost forecasts, and financial controls.&lt;br&gt;Track procurement schedules and mitigate supply chain risks.&lt;br&gt;• Review progress payment certifications and contractor claims.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure performance bond, insurance (CAR/EAR), and risk transfer compliance.&lt;br&gt;• Participate in tender evaluations and contract award recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;4.Team Leadership &amp;amp; stakeholder management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi-disciplinary project teams, contractors, consultants, and internal engineers.&lt;br&gt;Act as primary interface between clients, suppliers, utility authorities, and internal teams.&lt;br&gt;• Mentor junior engineers and project staff, fostering knowledge transfer and operational excellence.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure seamless communication and coordination across all stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;• Support Director of Engineering in strategic planning and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;5. Compliance, quality &amp;amp; safety&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce adherence to engineering standards, corporate governance, and safety regulations.&lt;br&gt;Conduct QA/QC inspections to validate system installation and workmanship.&lt;br&gt;• Support environmental, health, and safety (EHS) initiatives.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure environmental permits and statutory compliance are maintained throughout project lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 6.Operation and Handover&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate smooth transition to operations including as-built documentation, SOPs, MOPs, EOPs, and asset registers.&lt;br&gt;Ensure operational readiness, maintainability, and uptime SLA compliance.&lt;br&gt;• Support training of O&amp;amp;M teams and post-handover stabilization.&lt;br&gt;• Validate performance metrics including PUE, WUE, and system reliability KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job Functions &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/p&gt;
